 ∇ Example;conn;listing;entry;attrs;data;names
⍝ === SFTP Library — A Guided Tour ===
⍝
⍝ This function demonstrates every operation in the SFTP library.
⍝ It connects to a server, creates files and directories, reads them
⍝ back, and cleans up after itself.
⍝
⍝ To run:  ]link.import # path/to/SFTP.apln
⍝          ]link.import # path/to/Example.aplf
⍝          Example

⍝ ── Connecting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ Two ways to connect: password or key file.
⍝
⍝   conn ← SFTP.ConnectWithPass 'host' 22 'user' 'password'
⍝   conn ← SFTP.ConnectWithKey  'host' 22 'user' '/path/to/key' ''
⍝
⍝ Both return an opaque connection namespace. All subsequent
⍝ operations take this as their first argument.

   conn←SFTP.ConnectWithKey '89.167.123.234' 22 'root' '/tmp/aplsftp-test-key' ''
   ⎕←'Connected.'

⍝ ── Listing a directory ─────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ List returns a vector of (name, attrs) pairs.
⍝ attrs is a 7-element vector: flags filesize uid gid permissions atime mtime

   listing←SFTP.List conn '/'
   ⎕←'Root has ',(⍕≢listing),' entries: ',⍕⊃¨listing

⍝ ── Stat ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ Stat returns a namespace with: flags filesize uid gid permissions atime mtime

   attrs←SFTP.Stat conn '/etc/hostname'
   ⎕←'hostname file: ',(⍕attrs.filesize),' bytes, permissions ',(⍕attrs.permissions)

⍝ ── Creating a workspace ────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ Mkdir creates a directory. We'll make a temporary workspace.

   SFTP.Mkdir conn '/tmp/sftp-example'
   ⎕←'Created /tmp/sftp-example'

⍝ ── Writing files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ Put writes data to a remote path. It accepts:
⍝   - a character vector (automatically encoded as UTF-8)
⍝   - a byte vector (integer 0–255, written as-is)
⍝ Upload reads a local file and writes it to a remote path.

   SFTP.Put conn 'Shakespeare wrote in APL.' '/tmp/sftp-example/claim.txt'
   SFTP.Put conn 'Proof: 2 + 2 ←→ 4'       '/tmp/sftp-example/proof.txt'
   ⎕←'Wrote two files.'

⍝ ── Reading files back ──────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ Get returns the file contents as a byte vector.
⍝ Download writes directly to a local file.

   data←SFTP.Get conn '/tmp/sftp-example/claim.txt'
   ⎕←'Read back: ','UTF-8'⎕UCS data

   SFTP.Download conn '/tmp/sftp-example/proof.txt' '/tmp/aplsftp-test/proof.txt'
   ⎕←'Downloaded proof.txt to /tmp/aplsftp-test/'

⍝ ── Listing our workspace ──────────────────────────────────────────

   listing←SFTP.List conn '/tmp/sftp-example'
   names←⊃¨listing
   names←(~names∊(,'.') '..')/names
   ⎕←'Our directory: ',⍕names

⍝ ── Renaming ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   SFTP.Rename conn '/tmp/sftp-example/claim.txt' '/tmp/sftp-example/retracted.txt'
   ⎕←'Renamed claim.txt → retracted.txt'

⍝ ── Verifying the rename ────────────────────────────────────────────

   listing←SFTP.List conn '/tmp/sftp-example'
   names←⊃¨listing
   names←(~names∊(,'.') '..')/names
   ⎕←'After rename: ',⍕names

⍝ ── Cleanup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝
⍝ Delete removes a file. Rmdir removes an empty directory.
⍝ We must remove all files before removing the directory.

   SFTP.Delete conn '/tmp/sftp-example/retracted.txt'
   SFTP.Delete conn '/tmp/sftp-example/proof.txt'
   SFTP.Rmdir conn '/tmp/sftp-example'
   ⎕←'Cleaned up.'

⍝ ── Disconnecting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

   SFTP.Disconnect conn
   ⎕←'Disconnected. Tour complete.'
 ∇
